IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part8`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part8.l4 (s 65, distance).  Expected values are written from the text: a straight line on a
-- horizontal plane, so a 3-4-5 triangle gives 5 and a difference in height changes nothing.

§ `Tests -- Part VIII (distance)`

GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A place on the ground`
`test place` e n h MEANS
    `A place on the ground` WITH
        `metres east of the datum`  IS e
        `metres north of the datum` IS n
        `metres above the datum`    IS h

#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 0 0 0) `and` (`test place` 3 4 0) EQUALS 5
-- the same two places with one of them 100 metres up a hill: still 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 0 0 0) `and` (`test place` 3 4 100) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 0 0 25) `and` (`test place` 3 4 (0 MINUS 40)) EQUALS 5
-- directly above one another: no horizontal distance
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 7 7 0) `and` (`test place` 7 7 50) EQUALS 0
-- symmetric, and negative offsets
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 3 4 0) `and` (`test place` 0 0 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` (0 MINUS 3) (0 MINUS 4) 0) `and` (`test place` 0 0 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 1 1 0) `and` (`test place` 4 5 10) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 0 0 0) `and` (`test place` 100 0 0) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the distance measured for the purposes of a written law between` (`test place` 0 0 0) `and` (`test place` 0 (0 MINUS 250) 0) EQUALS 250
